1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,225
The Carnival of Blood: a travelling show where some visitors never make it home.

2
00:00:04,445 --> 00:00:06,195
Here's how the location plays.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,499
Set the three Item Trap cards aside and shuffle the other Items.

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:15,288
Deal three face-down decks of two Items, add one Item Trap to each, and shuffle each

5
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:17,844
deck. Then put one Item face up on top of each.

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:22,272
Each Item deck hides one Item Trap, found only by searching.

7
00:00:22,492 --> 00:00:26,376
If you draw one, you must resolve it, unless something like Zappo protects you.

8
00:00:26,376 --> 00:00:29,916
If the search also found an Item, you can still take it, after the trap.

9
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:34,968
Three Terror cards are Terror Traps. When one is drawn, place its Trap token in your

10
00:00:34,968 --> 00:00:38,093
space: it hits you and kills any Victims there, straight away.

11
00:00:38,313 --> 00:00:42,318
Trap tokens stay for the rest of the game, and trigger whenever you or a Victim

12
00:00:42,318 --> 00:00:44,244
enter. Enemies ignore them completely.

13
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:48,693
A few tips. Zappo the monkey or Asami let you avoid Item Traps.

14
00:00:48,913 --> 00:00:52,497
Charlie can trade health for big Critical Blows once she's made her rescues.

15
00:00:52,717 --> 00:00:56,975
It's one of the hardest locations in logged games, so map where the Trap tokens

16
00:00:56,975 --> 00:00:57,837
land. Good luck.

